The  '''''International Journal of Molecular Sciences''''' is a [[peer-reviewed]] [[open access]] [[scientific journal]] covering research in [[chemistry]], [[molecular physics]], and [[molecular biology]]. It is published by [[MDPI]] and was established in 2000. The journal is considered one of MDPI's [[Flagship product|flagship]] publications.<ref name="Grove">{{cite journal |last1=Grove |first1=Jack |date=March 15, 2023 |title=3,514 Special Issues a Year? |url=https://www.insidehighered.com/news/2023/03/16/swiss-journal-publisher-raises-eyebrows-special-issues |journal=Inside Higher Ed |language=en}}</ref>

The [[editor-in-chief]] is Maurizio Battino ([[Marche Polytechnic University]]).<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mdpi.com/journal/ijms/editors/ |title=IJMS — Editors |access-date=2012-03-07}}</ref>  More than 1,000 people are on the journal's [[editorial board]].<ref name="Oviedo-García">{{cite journal |last=Ángeles Oviedo-García |first=Maria |date=11 August 2021 |title=Journal citation reports and the definition of a predatory journal: The case of the Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI) |url=https://academic.oup.com/rev/article/30/3/405/6348133 |journal=Research Evaluation |volume=30 |issue=3 |pages=405–419a |doi=10.1093/reseval/rvab030 |doi-access=free}}</ref>

== Special issues ==
In 2019, this journal published 500 [[Supplement (publishing)|special issues]].<ref name="Oviedo-García" />  According to Jack Grove in ''[[Inside Higher Ed]]'', it planned 3,514 "special issues with a closing date in 2023" – nearly 10 per day.<ref name="Grove" />

